reate-a-lambda-with-asynchronous-invocation-polling-invocation"></a>Sub-tas=
k 1 - Create a Lambda with Asynchronous Invocation (Polling Invocation)</h3=
>
<ol data-sourcepos=3D"21:1-30:0" dir=3D"auto">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"21:1-23:193">Create a Lambda function named <em data-=
sourcepos=3D"21:35-21:79">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-UploadsNotificationFunction</=
em>:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"22:4-23:193">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"22:4-22:43">use any preferred programming language</l=
i>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"23:4-23:193">grant the function the basic Lambda perm=
issions as well as permissions for sending messages to <em data-sourcepos=
=3D"23:101-23:142">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-UploadsNotificationTopic</em> from t=
he <a data-sourcepos=3D"23:153-23:193" href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-ac=
m-public/aws-associate-training/-/blob/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_=
Developer/tasks/sns_sqs/README.md" class=3D"gfm">Module 9: SNS/SQS</a>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"24:1-24:85">Remove the code from the web-application =
that transfers SQS messages to SNS topic.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"25:1-28:165">Add a Lambda trigger:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"26:4-28:165">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"26:4-26:167">make sure that execution role of the Lam=
bda contains permissions for the <em data-sourcepos=3D"26:79-26:120">&lt;Pr=
ojectName&gt;-UploadsNotificationQueue</em> from <a data-sourcepos=3D"26:12=
7-26:167" href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-traini=
ng/-/blob/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/sns_sqs/READM=
E.md" class=3D"gfm">Module 9: SNS/SQS</a>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"27:4-27:68">choose <em data-sourcepos=3D"27:13-27:54"=
>&lt;ProjectName&gt;-UploadsNotificationQueue</em> as SQS source</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"28:4-28:165">update the lambda code and implement sen=
ding messages to the <em data-sourcepos=3D"28:67-28:108">&lt;ProjectName&gt=
;-UploadsNotificationTopic</em> topic (this logic was removed from your web=
-application)</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"29:1-30:0">Make 2 or more image uploads using your we=
b application. Ensure you got exactly emails with all the publications you=
=E2=80=99ve just made.</li>
</ol>
<h3 data-sourcepos=3D"31:1-31:60" dir=3D"auto">
<a href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/-/bl=
ob/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/serverless/README.md=
#sub-task-2---create-a-lambda-with-synchronous-invocation" aria-hidden=3D"t=
rue" class=3D"anchor" id=3D"user-content-sub-task-2---create-a-lambda-with-=
synchronous-invocation"></a>Sub-task 2 - Create a Lambda with Synchronous I=
nvocation</h3>
<ol data-sourcepos=3D"33:1-45:0" dir=3D"auto">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"33:1-35:197">Create a Lambda function named <em data-=
sourcepos=3D"33:35-33:75">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-DataConsistencyFunction</em>:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"34:4-35:197">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"34:4-34:43">use any preferred programming language</l=
i>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"35:4-35:197">grant the function the basic Lambda perm=
issions as well as permissions to have access to the DB from <a data-source=
pos=3D"35:107-35:139" href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-asso=
ciate-training/-/blob/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/r=
ds/README.md" class=3D"gfm">Module 8: RDS</a> and to the S3 bucket from <a =
data-sourcepos=3D"35:167-35:197" href=3D"https://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-publ=
ic/aws-associate-training/-/blob/master/courses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Develo=
per/tasks/s3/README.md" class=3D"gfm">Module 4: S3</a>
</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"36:1-38:109">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"36:4-36:16">Important</strong>: To ensure secure =
and private communication:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"37:4-38:109">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"37:4-37:113">Create a VPC Endpoint for S3 to allow La=
mbda to access the S3 bucket without traversing the public internet.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"38:4-38:109">Ensure the Lambda function resides in th=
e same VPC as the RDS instance so it can securely access the DB.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"39:1-39:248">Implement some basic validation that ver=
ifies that DB metadata corresponds to the images in the S3 bucket (you can =
add some simple validation like finding image by name). The lambda should r=
eturn a result that shows if data is consistent or not.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"40:1-40:141">
<strong data-sourcepos=3D"40:4-40:16">Important</strong> Please keep in min=
d best practices of writing lambda code. Initializing connection to the DB =
should be outside the function.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"41:1-41:142">Create an endpoint in your web applicati=
on which would do the same =E2=80=93 simply trigger the <em data-sourcepos=
=3D"41:94-41:134">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-DataConsistencyFunction</em> Lambda.<=
/li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"42:1-42:177">Follow <a data-sourcepos=3D"42:11-42:108=
" href=3D"https://docs.aws.amazon.com/AmazonCloudWatch/latest/events/RunLam=
bdaSchedule.html" rel=3D"nofollow noreferrer noopener" target=3D"_blank">th=
is tutorial</a> to make your Lambda run periodically (let=E2=80=99s say, ev=
ery 5 minutes).</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"43:1-43:373">Make your Lambda logs scheduled/API Gate=
way/web application calls in such a way that it=E2=80=99s possible to disti=
nguish them in the CloudWatch logs. <strong data-sourcepos=3D"43:149-43:156=
">Hint</strong> =E2=80=93 the tutorial from step 6 makes the Lambda receive=
 messages which have a <em data-sourcepos=3D"43:234-43:246">detail-type</em=
> field, so it=E2=80=99s possible to fill that field differently for the ca=
lls made from the web application and API Gateway endpoint.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"44:1-45:0">Make sure you can see all 3 (scheduled/API=
 Gateway/web application) kinds of Lambda calls in the CloudWatch logs.</li=
>
</ol>
<h3 dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"46:1-46:72">
<a id=3D"user-content-sub-task-3---create-a-lambda-with-asynchronous-invoca=
tion-optional" class=3D"anchor" aria-hidden=3D"true" href=3D"https://git.ep=
am.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/-/blob/master/courses/CloudX_=
Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/serverless/README.md#sub-task-3---create-a-la=
mbda-with-asynchronous-invocation-optional"></a>Sub-task 3 - Create a Lambd=
a with Asynchronous Invocation (Optional)</h3>
<ol dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"48:1-55:0">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"48:1-50:52">Create a Lambda function named <em data-s=
ourcepos=3D"48:35-48:66">&lt;ProjectName&gt;-S3LogsFunction</em>:
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"49:4-50:52">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"49:4-49:43">use any preferred programming language</l=
i>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"50:4-50:52">grant the function the basic Lambda permi=
ssions</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"51:1-51:124">Update an execution role of the lambda t=
o contain the permissions for the S3 bucket from <a class=3D"gfm" href=3D"h=
ttps://git.epam.com/epmc-acm-public/aws-associate-training/-/blob/master/co=
urses/CloudX_Associate_AWS_Developer/tasks/s3/README.md" data-sourcepos=3D"=
51:93-51:123">Module 4: S3</a>.</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"52:1-53:159">Configure your S3 image bucket to send o=
bject creation events to that Lambda.
<ul data-sourcepos=3D"53:4-53:159">
<li data-sourcepos=3D"53:4-53:159">Tip: Since the Lambda handler code is ex=
tremely simple, you may code it directly in the AWS Console using any of th=
e available scripting language options.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li data-sourcepos=3D"54:1-55:0">Upload an image to your S3 bucket and ensu=
re you can see the Lambda reacts to this in CloudWatch logs.</li>
</ol>
<h2 dir=3D"auto" data-sourcepos=3D"56:1-56:26">
<a id=3D"user-content-what-should-i-remember" class=3D"anchor" aria-hidden=
